# Quantum monorepo

Two products share this repository:

- **`agent/`** — Agent Manager (Bun, Effect, React). Follow [agent/AGENTS.md](../../agent/AGENTS.md).
- **`ide/`** — Quantum IDE (VS Code fork). Follow [ide/AGENTS.md](../../ide/AGENTS.md).

Root orchestration: `npm ci` (Turbo), `./scripts/setup.sh`, `./scripts/verify.sh` ([monorepo-orchestration.md](../../docs/architecture/monorepo-orchestration.md)). **Do not** merge `ide/` and `agent/` into one package-manager workspace — IDE stays npm, Agent stays Bun.

Documentation hub: [docs/readme.md](../../docs/readme.md) · agent routing: [docs/for-agents.md](../../docs/for-agents.md).

Git / editor policy: [docs/version-control.md](../../docs/version-control.md). Run `./scripts/verify-repo-config.sh` when changing root `.gitignore`, `.cursor/`, `.idea/`, or `.vscode/`.

When editing:

- Touch only the product tree that matches the task; avoid cross-imports between `agent/` and `ide/`.
- In `ide/`, all agentic AI features (chat, inline edit, tools, MCP) belong exclusively in `ide/src/vs/workbench/contrib/agent/`. Never edit or confuse with upstream Microsoft Copilot directories (`contrib/chat`, `contrib/inlineChat`, `sessions`).
- Use `Quantum.code-workspace` or open `ide/` / `agent/` directly for product-specific VS Code tasks and debug configs.
- No telemetry; client-side privacy is a core invariant ([readme.md](../../readme.md)).
